      "question": "Do I need a visa for Mauritania?",
      "answer": "Most nationalities do. Since January 2025 you must apply online for an eVisa through the official ANRPTS portal before travel, then pay the fee — EUR 55 for 30 days, or EUR 40 for nationals of Arab and African countries — in cash on arrival. Citizens of eleven neighboring West African and Maghreb states (including Algeria, Tunisia, Senegal and Mali) enter visa-free under reciprocal agreements; the Foreign Ministry does not state how long they may stay."
